  "id": "Compound::DB00761 - Gene::6560",
  "verbalization": "Potassium Chloride is shown to interact with multiple members of the Slc12 family, specifically Slc12a5, Slc12a6, and Slc12a7, which are all involved in cation-coupled chloride cotransporters. These interactions suggest that Potassium Chloride may influence the function of these transporters, potentially through binding or modulatory effects. The evidence indicates that Slc12a4, a member of the same family, is a downstream participant in the cation-coupled chloride cotransporters, implying a possible role in the transport process. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent level of interaction, though slightly lower in path_2044. The mechanisms likely involve the regulation of chloride transport by Potassium Chloride, which could affect cellular ion homeostasis. The relationship between Potassium Chloride and Slc12a4 is supported by the observed pathway connections, though further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the functional significance of these interactions.",
